Dereference
description: the pull — * takes a path and yields a shared edge
- >
  `*path` **pulls**: "my value lives there". The `*` sigil is the authoring embedding of a path — the
  only thing that creates an edge — and it takes the full grammar: scopes, positions, escapes.
  Resolution is lazy and yields a **graph edge, never a copy**: the target node is shared, and a ref
  edge is never expanded inline to infinity, so cycles are safe.
- !!yo
  cat: furry manager supervising humans life
  feline: *cat        # the sibling key — one node, two paths
- >
  Walking *through* a pointer dereferences implicitly and transitively: a step into an entry whose
  value is a pointer yields the target node, cycle-safely — a path never stops halfway at "a pointer".
  On the json5p surface the same expression is quoted: `*'..: ..: pets: 1'`.
- >
  Pointers are the **singleton fragment of the query language**: every pointer is a valid query with
  at most one result — its resolved target, or nothing if dangling
  ([queries](::language:pointers:queries)). A dangling pointer is a diagnostic, never an error that
  refuses the document.
